course: dictionary
lesson: 1218
title: One word, three meanings: build
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word build has more than one meaning, so check the words around it. «The capital of Australia is Canberra, built as a compromise between Sydney and Melbourne.» Here build means made, put together from parts, like a city or a tower.
explain: Build can also mean to grow bigger or stronger, little by little. «Sharing silly jokes, like knock-knock jokes, builds friendship.» Nobody builds a friendship with one joke. It grows slowly, one shared laugh at a time.
explain: Build can be a noun too. Your build is the shape and size of your body, so a person with a sturdy build is solid and strong-looking. When you meet build, ask: is something being made, growing, or describing a body?
fact: To build something means to make it by putting parts together, like blocks, bricks or a model.
fact: «Build up» means to make bigger or stronger, little by little.
fact: Your build is the shape and size of your body.
fact: «Ukraine's black earth, chornozem, was built over thousands of years» means it formed slowly, over a very long time.
fact: In a story, the build-up is the part where things start to grow towards the problem.
exercise: «The children built a tower from wooden blocks.» What does built mean here? | Knocked down | Bought in a shop | Painted red | *Made by putting parts together
exercise: «Sharing silly jokes builds friendship.» What does builds mean here? | Hides | Forgets | *Makes something grow stronger, little by little | Breaks up
exercise: Priya says, «He has a sturdy build.» What does build mean? | *The shape and size of his body | A kind of bread | A game with cards | Going to bed early
test: «Canberra was built as a compromise between Sydney and Melbourne.» What is a compromise here? | A tall building | A kind of cake | A big fight | *A deal where each side gives a bit
test: Which phrase means to make bigger or stronger, little by little? | *Build up | Built of | Build a sandcastle | Knock down
exam: In a story mountain, what is the build-up? | The name of the main character | The very last page | A drawing on the cover | *The part that gets the story ready for the problem
